    49	## 1. Transaction and guarantees
    50	
    51	`begin` takes one explicit final path, basis commit, and owner. It performs no
    52	file discovery. An `O_EXCL` lease wins the canonical target, returns a random
    53	capability token and private partial path, rejects occupied final/manifest/
    54	close/release names, and probes same-directory hard-link support.
    55	
    56	The author writes only the returned partial. `close` requires that the file
    57	end exactly at the unique standalone `BODY-END` marker, removes write bits,
    58	fsyncs it, and records an exact content hash plus device/inode/mode/size/time
    59	snapshot. Repeated close is idempotent only when the frozen bytes still agree.
    60	
    61	`finalize` refuses unsealed drift, delegates the canonical seal bytes to
    62	`ops/seal.py`, and publishes the final report by a no-overwrite hard link. It
    63	publishes a canonical read-only JSON manifest containing full/body hashes,
    64	frozen basis, source custody, owner, and lifecycle times. A separate immutable
    65	release record commits the lease/close/publication hashes before cleanup, so
    66	interruptions after final publication, after manifest publication, or during
    67	cleanup are recoverable by rerunning `finalize` with the same token.
    68	
    69	`verify` checks canonical seal bytes, final and manifest hashes, basis, modes,
    70	repeat-read snapshots, and absence of lease/close/release residue. Optional
    71	`--staged` verification additionally requires unique stage-zero Git blobs for
    72	both report and manifest and rereads the files after the index query. Thus a
    73	staged commit can be bound to the bytes that passed verification.
    74	
    75	The regression suite covers competing writers, wrong tokens, pre-existing
    76	targets, post-close content drift, post-final content and mode drift,
    77	noncanonical post-seal content, idempotent close/finalize, final-only and
    78	manifest/release interruption recovery, cleanup quarantine, metadata-link
    79	interruptions, and Git-index mismatch.
